    14	# Design analysis for the D4 variant
    15	# ----------------------------------
    16	# concrete_behavior:
    17	#   clean scene:
    18	#     - black background plus exactly three large connected foreground regions
    19	#     - the three regions play stable spatial roles: left, right, bottom
    20	#     - each region has black dents and a few one-cell wrong-color specks
    21	#   output scene:
    22	#     - after cleanup, every dent becomes a 3x3 patch whose color follows a
    23	#       visible role cycle: left -> right, right -> bottom, bottom -> left
    24	#     - the dent center itself is teal
    25	#   small execution trace:
    26	#     - original task: a dent inside the green region always stamps the only
    27	#       other foreground color, say yellow
    28	#     - new task: a dent inside the left region does not use "the only other"
    29	#       color because there are two alternatives; instead it uses the color of
    30	#       the right region, while right dents use bottom and bottom dents use left
    31	#     - difference: the solver must infer three roles first, then map host role
    32	#       through a 3-cycle before stamping the 3x3 patch
    33	# complexity_calibration:
    34	#   - using three large regions keeps the main visual motif from the source task
    35	#   - role-based color mapping has only one branch pattern (a fixed cycle), so
    36	#     samples can repeat it enough for humans to infer it
    37	#   - the generator guarantees dents in all three regions, preventing collapse
    38	#     back to an effectively two-region training signal
    39	# implicit_assumption_audit:
    40	#   - old _main_colors assumed two colors; now the solver asserts three
    41	#   - old cleanup compared a cell only against one "other" color; now it checks
    42	#     for any unique dominant rival among three colors
    43	#   - old dent stamping used host -> unique other-color; now it uses host-role
    44	#     -> mapped role color, so role inference must happen before stamping
    45	# placement_legality:
    46	#   - generator paints three large rectangles in fixed spatial roles so the
    47	#     centroid-based role inference is stable
    48	#   - dent centers are chosen only where the host color is the unique 3x3
    49	#     majority even after the center is removed
    50	#   - noise is added with local legality checks and every sample is still
    51	#     validated once by the full solver at the end
    52	# visual_observability:
    53	#   - the rule never depends on color ids or area ranking
    54	#   - role identity is visible from position, and each sample contains all three
    55	#     host colors producing dents, so the cycle is observable from examples
    56	# neatness:
    57	#   - only one overlay layer is added per dent (3x3 patch + teal center)
    58	#   - patches are separated by Chebyshev distance >= 3, limiting clutter
